                        <addName>Count Maceroni</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1788">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1846"/>
                    <occupation>soldier</occupation>
                    <occupation>mechanical inventor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Maceroni was a soldier, exiled Italian, inventor and author.  According to Margaret Wicks, <title>Italians in Exile</title>, he was a member of the Society of European 
    Constitutionalists, aiming for a complete revolution in Italy. He published his memoirs in 1838.</p>
                        <p>There is an entry noting 'G Macirone' also in 1824 which may be his wife or a relative.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Margaret Wicks, <title>The Italian Exiles in London, 1816-1848</title> (Manchester: Manchester University Press, 1937)</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Marizion Isabella, <title>The Risorgimento in Exile</title> (Oxford, Oxford University Press, 2009)</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Francis Maceroni, <title>Memoirs of the life and adventures of Colonel Maceroni</title> (London, 1838)</bibl>
